{"event_type":"finding-event","id":"6cbec91cd74a8e904bf958f3479b2b88e4f8a96bd608094be32ff226bfaa27ed","occurred_at":"2026-11-21T19:58:06Z","payload":{"action":"confirmed","actor":"crq-triage/opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash","evidence":{"anchor_verified":true,"failure_class":"evidence","mapped_intervals":[[90,94]],"mapped_path":"apps/crq-python/test_deploy_runbook.py","quoted_text":"        self.command(\"init\", \"-q\")\n        self.command(\"config\", \"user.email\", \"fixture@example.invalid\")\n        self.command(\"config\", \"user.name\", \"Fixture\")\n        self.command(\"add\", \".\")\n        self.command(\"commit\", \"-qm\", \"baseline\")","reason":"The fixture creates a temporary git repository, sets a synthetic committer identity, and commits without disabling inherited commit.gpgSign. If global config enables commit signing, git attempts to sign with no matching key for fixture@example.invalid, so the baseline commit fails and DeployFixture.setUp errors. Setting repository-local commit.gpgSign=false before the first commit is the smallest compatible fix and also affects the later fixture commit.","target":"1a24298c224d98c22de0e771807d89568668ec61"},"finding_id":"e995dceaf9b76b1da702b27d63ab7d33bc30f60a12534ecc499fec178d76c123","previous_event_id":"480d3f093103838060eab254236d4322a6447f5eaf37d62d970e2972487cac1c","review_id":"21962c553cc8f4551c5b1c09bd030ad284c93562b7a36e530e11a83b5391f5ad"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"finding:e995dceaf9b76b1da702b27d63ab7d33bc30f60a12534ecc499fec178d76c123:f2a658004894aef0b48d88662b028a6f71b1665a6f8ad42b81145a10bcbf458f"}